          { name: "Overlooking the Demographic Gap as Strategic Irrelevance", tag: "avoid", why: "The ~5.6% population segment not captured in the reported Census categories is sufficiently large in a 36-point margin to suggest it exists and has not been fully mobilized in either direction; assuming this population is either nonexistent or electorally irrelevant is a strategic error. A challenger who invests resources in understanding and mobilizing this community — whether AIAN, Hispanic, or other — around issues where the incumbent's record is weak could shift several percentage points and move MT-HD-21 from a 68-32 seat to something far more competitive." }
