          "Lead with rural healthcare and cost-of-living security: at median age 48.2 and income $55,808, the constituency is aging into higher healthcare costs and facing rising property taxes and service delivery challenges in a rural geography. Specific legislative achievements on rural hospital viability, healthcare access for older adults, and property tax relief are the tangible constituent services that prevent economic anxiety from translating into opposition.",
          "Engage the 32.6% renter constituency with intentional policy attention: renters in rural Montana face distinct housing cost pressures, limited service access, and economic mobility constraints compared to homeowners, and they represent nearly one-third of the district. A representative who addresses renter needs alongside homeowner priorities demonstrates governance of the actual district rather than governance of the homeowner supermajority.",
          "Investigate and serve the ~4% demographic gap: American Indian, Alaska Native, Hispanic, or other communities present in the district but underrepresented in Census reporting deserve constituent attention and legislative responsiveness. Building authentic relationships with these populations is both a governance obligation and a potential electoral asset if a challenger attempts to activate them as opposition."
