          "Lead with working-class economic security: at $61,449 income with 35.1% renter rate, focus legislative attention on housing affordability, healthcare cost management, and property tax fairness — the material concerns most likely to activate a future challenger if ignored.",
          "Identify and engage the 7.17% demographic gap with specificity: determine whether it represents American Indian / Alaska Native residents, whether they are connected to organized tribal communities, and what their governance expectations are — ensuring that any constituent relationship is built on actual demographic understanding rather than omission.",
          "Monitor economic trends in younger adult cohorts: the 42.6 median age and modest college attainment suggest a district without strong youth retention; any outmigration of young adults to larger cities for economic opportunity is a sign that future challenges may come from candidates promising different economic development strategies."
