          "Build authentic partnership with the Native American majority (likely 63%+ of the district): the largest demographic gap in this brief signals a community whose healthcare, economic development, and tribal sovereignty concerns are not being adequately measured in the 53% result. Engagement here is both a governance obligation and the most direct path to consolidating the incumbent's margin or flipping the seat if you are the challenger.",
          "Address the education attainment gap directly: at 20.9% college attainment, this district has the lowest educational engagement in the sequence. Early childhood education, K-12 funding, vocational training, and pathways to skilled employment are the material issues that affect younger adults' ability to earn above subsistence wage. This is not abstract education policy — it is economic mobility.",
          "Understand whether the 47% opposition is concentrated among Native American voters, younger renters, or both — and whether it reflects active dissatisfaction or insufficient incumbent engagement. The margin is too close and the district too young to assume the 53% is stable; treating this as a safe seat rather than a genuinely competitive one is the most likely path to losing it."
