          { name: "Education Funding, K-12 Quality, and Higher Education Access", tag: "lean-into", why: "With 57.5% college attainment and a 43.3 median age, a large share of this district's households have children in schools or recent experience with higher education decisions. Education funding adequacy, teacher compensation, and higher education affordability are practical governance questions with direct household relevance. A legislative agenda demonstrating concrete commitment to education investment and quality is more persuasive to this constituency than abstract conservative positioning." },
          { name: "Understanding the 47% Opposition in an Affluent, Educated Constituency", tag: "careful", why: "A 53% Democratic result in Montana's political environment represents a genuine coalition across a district that should demographically favor Republicans. The 47% opposition is not explained by income inequality or educational access but by specific policy disagreements with college-educated, affluent voters who are choosing the Democrat deliberately. Any candidate must understand whether the opposition is concentrated in opposition to tax policy, environmental regulation, healthcare approach, or other specific governance concerns — and address those concerns directly rather than assuming the 53% margin is stable without active engagement." },
          { name: "Treating This District as a Safe Partisan Hold", tag: "avoid", why: "A 53% margin in a state where Republicans control statewide offices is not a majority — it is a plurality of voters in a constituency that is genuinely swing-capable. Any incumbent or challenger who campaigns assuming inherited partisan loyalty will discover that educated, affluent, pragmatic voters are willing to evaluate both candidates and switch if they conclude the incumbent is not delivering for them. This district requires active constituent engagement and demonstrated results, not partisan confidence." },
          { name: "Relying on Cultural or Partisan Messaging Rather Than Governance Solutions", tag: "avoid", why: "MT-HD-46's demographic profile — 92.72% white, affluent, educated — might suggest receptiveness to cultural conservative messaging. However, the 53-47 result demonstrates that this constituency is evaluating candidates on competence and policy solutions, not identity politics or cultural positioning. Any candidate who leads with cultural or partisan appeals rather than credible governance answers will find this constituency unmoved and the 47% opposition mobilized." }
