          "Engage education and workforce development with specific attention to cost and outcomes: the 29% college-educated rate in a young district signals constituents actively evaluating whether education investments deliver economic mobility, and both higher education affordability and technical training pathways are concrete policy areas where candidates must show understanding.",
          "Do not assume the 57% represents durable Republican support: a young, renting, working-class constituency evaluates on material economic outcomes, not inherited partisan loyalty. Any incumbent must actively maintain support through specific engagement on the issues that matter to people aged 25-45 in their financial lifecycle.",
          "Understand opposition concentration: identify specifically whether the 43% opposition is concentrated among renters frustrated by housing costs, among younger voters doubting economic opportunity, or distributed across the district. Mobilizing opposition turnout among young, renting voters has historically proven sufficient to flip competitive seats in resource-constrained regions."
