          "Understand the 24% opposition as a constituency worth engaging: one-quarter of MT-HD-53 voters actively chose Democratic representation in 2024; they are not marginal or illegitimate, and a candidate who treats them as beneath engagement is missing an opportunity to strengthen the seat's underlying legitimacy across the full spectrum of the district's voters.",
          "Lead on specific material concerns of high-income homeowners: property tax sustainability, K-12 education funding and accountability, water rights and natural resource stewardship, rural infrastructure, and regulatory environment for small business and professional services — these are the real governance issues that this constituency cares about and that distinguish effective representation from mere partisan confirmation.",
          "Avoid abstract conservative positioning in favor of concrete problem-solving: this is not a constituency motivated by ideological purity or culture-war messaging, but by whether government is delivering measurable results on their material interests — responsive constituent service, transparent budgeting, and evidence-based policy are more persuasive to affluent professionals than partisan rhetoric."
