          { name: "Ignoring the Renter Constituency's Distinct Economic Concerns", tag: "avoid", why: "At 42.6% renter rate, nearly half the district experiences the economy differently than homeowners—rent costs rather than mortgage payments, no equity accumulation, and exposure to market-driven housing costs—and these constituents' concerns around affordability, stability, and development policy require specific legislative attention rather than homeowner-focused agenda prioritization. Treating renters as a temporary constituency or secondary concern relative to homeowner interests misses that college-educated younger renters are likely swing voters who evaluate candidates on whether housing policy serves their material interests. An incumbent who ignores renter-specific concerns invites a challenger to mobilize this plurality with direct messaging about affordability and opportunity." }
