          { name: "Assuming Partisan Loyalty Among Older Homeowners", tag: "avoid", why: "Older, affluent, educated homeowners in MT-HD-58 are not voting Democratic because of inherited partisan loyalty—they are evaluating on specific governance performance and issue alignment. Any candidate whose strategy assumes that 'older homeowners eventually vote Republican' or that 'education and income should produce Republican margins' is operating from false premises about how this constituency actually decides. These voters have already demonstrated that demographic expectation is not their primary voting driver; campaigns must engage them on the specific issues that have convinced them to choose Democratic representation despite affluence and homeownership." }
