          "Build a persuasive economic mobility agenda for early-career professionals: the combination of 53.5% college education, $72,741 income, and 25.0 median age signals a constituency invested in wage growth, student debt relief, and career pathway clarity. A representative who can demonstrate that entry-level wages are rising and that young professionals can build assets in this district has a durable coalition; one who cannot will face a credible challenger in the next cycle.",
          "Do not assume college-educated voters are automatically loyal to either party: the 53.5% college attainment is high, but college-educated voters in a young, working-class-weighted district may evaluate differently than college-educated voters in higher-income areas. Some will prioritize student debt policy and wage floors; others will prioritize business-friendly regulation and lower taxes. Precision targeting matters more than broad demographic category messaging.",
