          { name: "Treating 100% Victory as Durable Floor", tag: "avoid", why: "An unopposed election is the easiest condition under which to become unresponsive, and unresponsiveness is the opening a challenger uses to gain credibility in an otherwise stable district. The 100% result does not indicate that the district is permanently secured—it indicates that no challenger emerged in 2024, not that no credible alternative exists or could emerge. A representative who assumes 100% is a durable baseline rather than a warning signal to establish constituent engagement infrastructure will find that the next competitive election tests the actual foundations of support, which may be weaker than the numbers suggest." },
          { name: "Generic Republican Positioning Without Local Issue Specificity", tag: "avoid", why: "A district of educated (36.9% college), affluent ($72,790 income), older (48.1 median age) homeowners does not evaluate primarily on inherited partisan loyalty—these voters have the education and economic stability to make deliberative choices based on local issue performance. A representative who campaigns and governs with generic conservative positioning on national issues rather than specific local policy responses to aging-in-place economics, property tax burden, rural healthcare, and broadband access will appear disconnected from constituent needs. A challenger who articulates specific local policy alternatives on these issues will credibly position themselves as more attentive to the district's actual governance concerns, regardless of the incumbent's 100% result in an unopposed cycle." }
