          "Engage the aging homeowner constituency on economic security: at 48.1 median age and 72.8k income with 85% homeownership, property tax burden, Medicare sustainability, and rural hospital viability are the material concerns that will activate opposition if unaddressed—lead with these issues, not generic Republican positioning.",
          "Identify and neutralize the next challenger's opening before they exploit it: a district this politically uniform and homogeneous will be attractive to a challenger only if they identify a specific governance failure—whether rural broadband, agricultural policy, or healthcare access—so establish a reputation for addressing these issues with specificity and prevent an alternative from claiming superior constituent focus.",
          "Do not mistake 100% for invincibility: unopposed victory is the easiest condition under which to become unresponsive, and an unresponsive incumbent in a district of educated homeowners is a target—the next election will test whether you have built the constituent relationship foundation that makes a seat genuinely durable."
