          "Engage the 38% opposition directly and specifically — in a district this politically cohesive, the opposition represents a real constituency with legitimate concerns about Democratic governance; understanding whether their frustration is rooted in economic stress, healthcare system failures, or specific policy disagreements is the first step toward either consolidating the Democratic hold or identifying genuine governance gaps.",
          "Maintain active partnership with the AIAN community (the ~4.3% demographic gap): though smaller than in rural Montana districts, this constituency deserves genuine engagement on tribal sovereignty, healthcare access, and economic development — not as a separate outreach effort, but as part of the district's broader civic fabric.",
          "Protect against economic anxiety driving defection: as cost-of-living pressures mount for middle-income households, a Democratic incumbent who does not demonstrate concrete delivery on healthcare affordability, housing costs, and property tax fairness risks having the 62% margin erode to a challenger who speaks directly to material household concerns."
