          { name: "Focusing Exclusively on College-Educated Coalition Building", tag: "avoid", why: "While the college-educated population is the margin of victory, they represent only 42.3% of the district — focusing campaign messaging and constituent service exclusively on college-educated professional constituencies while neglecting the 57.7% non-college-educated homeowner majority creates the conditions for erosion among the larger population group. The non-college-educated homeowners who currently lean Democratic are the actual swing constituency; they are voting against their demographic type and require specific messaging about how Democratic governance serves their material interests. Any strategy that treats non-college-educated voters as a fixed base rather than as persuadable constituencies vulnerable to economic messaging will lose the margin." }
