          "Engage homeowner constituencies directly on property tax management, school quality as a neighborhood and family concern, land-use decisions, and local service reliability; the 81.6% homeownership rate and 44.8-year median age signal voters with skin in the game who need to know you understand their stakes.",
          "Address working-class and renting minorities explicitly: the 69.5% without four-year degrees and 18.4% renters have real concerns around wage adequacy, job training, housing affordability, and healthcare access that differ from professional and homeowner priorities — neglecting them is both a representation failure and an electoral vulnerability.",
          "Do not assume 61% is a floor; it is a contingent result dependent on Keogh's specific alignment with the professional and homeowner constituencies that comprise it — any challenger who can demonstrate superior competence on these groups' material concerns, or any incumbent who takes this margin as secure absent active engagement, will find this seat more competitive than the result suggests."
