          "Engage the ~8.8% Native American constituency with authentic partnership on tribal economic development, Indian Health Service access, and state-tribal coordination on education and workforce development; this is not a special interest to be managed but a swing constituency whose participation likely explains the 62% margin and whose disengagement would immediately threaten the seat.",
          "Do not assume that a 62-38 result represents a durable majority: the combination of working-class white voters evaluating on economic performance and a Native American swing constituency means that either demographic group's shift of 4-6 percentage points would materially alter the outcome in the next cycle.",
          "Identify and specifically address what generated Democratic support among working-class white homeowners in a district that demographically should lean conservative; whether it is rural healthcare frustration with Republican governance, economic anxiety about housing and healthcare costs, or something else, naming it and solving it is necessary to consolidation."
