          "Demonstrate fiscal competence and cost-of-living responsiveness: the $75,954 income places this district in the upper-middle range where voters notice inflation, property taxes, and whether government spending is efficient; an incumbent who campaigns only on education funding without addressing cost pressures will find less enthusiasm among renters (37.8%) and younger professionals facing housing affordability.",
          "Maintain consistent presence and constituent service among the 37.8% renter population: renters are more mobile, less habitual voters, and more likely to shift if they perceive the representative as serving homeowners or wealthy interests at their expense; regular engagement on tenant protections, housing affordability, and service-sector workforce concerns keeps this swing portion of the base mobilized.",
          "Avoid the assumption that a 22-point margin is durable without active consolidation: a 61-39 result is commanding in a single cycle but reflects specific constituency choices that require ongoing reinforcement; any incumbent who takes this margin as evidence of a safe hold rather than a baseline to defend risks finding it narrowed by a challenger who takes education quality and fiscal responsibility seriously."
