          { name: "Assuming a 60-40 Margin Is Durable or Indicates Partisan Conversion", tag: "avoid", why: "While Cunningham's 60% is a clear 2024 victory, treating it as evidence of permanent Democratic dominance or genuine partisan realignment in MT-HD-97 is strategically premature. A single election cycle with a specific candidate does not establish trajectory; it establishes a data point. If the Democratic margin reflects Cunningham's personal credibility or a specific 2024 issue, a well-positioned Republican challenger running in 2026 or beyond could feasibly consolidate the baseline Republican constituency and compete seriously for the college-educated swing voters. Overconfident Democratic assumption of durability or overconfident Republican resignation both risk missing the genuine competitive opportunity in this district." }
