          "Lead on fiscal responsibility and education quality for college-educated homeowners: at $88,742 income with 35.7% college attainment, this constituency evaluates on whether schools are competitive, property taxes are reasonable, and government is efficiently run—not ideology, but performance and material outcomes for their families.",
          "Engage the professional economy specifically: the income and education levels suggest a workforce tied to healthcare, professional services, education, or technology sectors; understanding what these workers need from state policy—workforce development, business environment, professional licensing—is more relevant than generic Republican positioning.",
          "Do not assume 60% Democratic in a high-income, college-educated district is permanent; it is a 2024 result tied to either specific candidate strength or genuine issue-based realignment—either way, it is contestable in the next cycle with a credible Republican who understands the constituency's actual material concerns."
