          "Engage the 46% opposition as a legitimate Missoula constituency, not a turnout problem: this is a college town where the opposition is geographically present, educationally credible, and voting on local issues alongside the incumbent's base. Treating them as frivolous or dismissing their concerns activates them as an organized coalition.",
          "Do not assume the 54-46 result is a durable majority: it is a narrow plurality in a district where educated renters and younger voters have material grievances, and where the opposition can organize around housing costs and university priorities. The next cycle in MT-SD-24 will be contested on the ground, not decided by demographics."
