          "Address the renter constituency directly: 33.3% renter rate is well above Montana rural norms and signals young professionals, early-career workers, and others for whom housing costs and rental market stability are material concerns. Do not default to homeowner-centric messaging in a district where one-third of households are renters.",
          "Engage the tribal community with specificity: the demographic gap suggests meaningful Native American population; understand which nation(s) are represented geographically and engage their governance priorities — healthcare access, economic development, and educational opportunity — as constituent concerns, not symbolic acknowledgments.",
          "Treat 52-48 as genuinely competitive: a 4-point margin in a district with this education and income level is not a floor for incumbents or a ceiling for challengers. The margin reflects active evaluation by educated voters; any candidate who campaigns as though this district is safely partisan will lose voters who are genuinely undecided."
