          "Do not divide homeowners and renters — unite them around shared housing cost pressure. A 39% renter rate is substantial; a candidate who treats renters as an afterthought while consolidating homeowner support will leave a swing constituency unorganized.",
          "Recognize that 55% is contested, not secure: in Montana's current environment, this seat is genuinely competitive and will be won or lost on whether the suburban middle evaluates the incumbent as solving their problems, not on inherited partisan alignment."
