          "Address aging homeowner economic security directly: at $66,380 income and 52.1-year median age, this constituency faces rising healthcare costs, property tax pressures, and questions about Social Security and Medicare sustainability — specific policy responses on these issues outperform generic Republican messaging in districts this educated and this old.",
          "Maintain authentic engagement with the ~4.4% AIAN population and any other minority communities through concrete constituent service rather than assumption of electoral invisibility; even in overwhelmingly white districts, demographic minorities have real governance needs and can organize opposition if neglected over multiple election cycles.",
          "Do not treat the 68% as permission to disengage from the 32%: understand specifically whether the Democratic opposition comes from college-educated voters frustrated with partisan rigidity, from younger renters (27% of the district) with different economic priorities, or from specific local governance failures — and offer concrete answers rather than partisan repetition."
