          "Recognize that the 72% margin, while comfortable, reflects strong base alignment in a red state, not an insurmountable structural advantage — any Democratic challenger who can improve on the 28% by targeting economic anxiety among older fixed-income households or mobilizing the Native American community could narrow the margin significantly in a competitive cycle.",
