          "Olsen's 73% result indicates the incumbent has successfully consolidated college-educated, urban, younger voters into a stable Democratic coalition — any challenger must either expand Democratic turnout beyond the incumbent's base (difficult given the margin) or persuade a subset of the incumbent's voters that they have been specifically failed on an issue the incumbent has neglected.",
          "Given the small margins available (27% Republican baseline), a Republican holding strategy in MT-SD-48 is not viable; the focus must be on whether internal Democratic challenges or specific governance failures create a primary or general-election opportunity — otherwise, this is a seat to concede and allocate resources to competitive districts elsewhere."
